.TH IPHONEBRIDGE 1 "@DATE@" "iphonebridge @VERSION@" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
iphonebridge \- iPhone messages, notifications, contacts and calls over Bluetooth
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B iphonebridge
.I command
.RI [ options ]
.RI [ arguments ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B iphonebridge
bridges a paired iPhone to the Linux desktop over the standard Bluetooth
profiles MAP (messages), PBAP (contacts), ANCS (per\-app notifications)
and HFP (calls) \- no Mac relay, no cloud service.
.PP
A background daemon (a systemd user service) holds the Bluetooth
sessions and surfaces events as desktop notifications, an append\-only
history, and a D\-Bus service. This command starts that daemon, checks
its prerequisites, and talks to it. The graphical front end is
.BR iphonebridge-ui (1).
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B run
Run the daemon in the foreground until Ctrl+C or SIGTERM. The systemd
unit uses this; run it directly only for debugging.
.TP
.B doctor
Check prerequisites: configuration, the adapter's Class of Device,
obexd, the state directory, BLE advertising (a live register/release
probe) and whether the iPhone's bond exposes ANCS. Exits non\-zero if a
required check fails.
.TP
.B pair-setup
First\-run wizard: pick a paired iPhone, write the local configuration,
and walk through the iPhone\-side toggles. With
.B \-\-no\-restart
the daemon is not restarted at the end.
.TP
.B sms-list
Show recent SMS/iMessage history.
.RS
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-limit " " \fIN\fR
Maximum messages to show, most recent first.
.TP
.BR \-\-source " " iphone | local
.B iphone
(default) queries the phone live over MAP through the running daemon;
.B local
reads the daemon's own history file and works with the daemon stopped.
.TP
.BR \-\-folder " " \fIFOLDER\fR
MAP folder for \-\-source=iphone, e.g. telecom/msg/INBOX (default) or
telecom/msg/sent.
.TP
.BR \-\-from " " \fIWHO\fR
Only messages from this contact name or number.
.RE
.TP
.BI sms-send " RECIPIENT BODY"
Send an SMS or iMessage through the running daemon.
.I RECIPIENT
is a phone number, a contact name, or a vanity number such as
"1 (800) MYAPPLE". iOS routes the message as iMessage automatically
when the recipient is iMessage\-capable.
.TP
.BI call " RECIPIENT"
Place a phone call over HFP; same recipient forms as
.BR sms-send .
Requires
.B hfp-enable
setup. Call audio uses this computer's microphone and speakers.
.TP
.B calls
List active calls.
.TP
.B hangup
Hang up all active calls.
.TP
.B contacts-sync
Re\-pull the phonebook (otherwise refreshed daily). With the daemon
running the pull reuses its sessions; the iPhone allows only one OBEX
session at a time.
.TP
.B ancs-enable
Enable per\-app notifications. Steers the next connection to the iPhone
over BLE by setting BlueZ's experimental PreferredBearer control, then
reconnects; answer the allow\-notifications prompt that appears on the
phone. Requires "Experimental = true" in /etc/bluetooth/main.conf and
an adapter capable of a BLE bond with the iPhone (Intel chipsets are;
Realtek and USB dongles are not).
.TP
.B hfp-enable
Set up call support: writes the WirePlumber configuration that routes
HFP through oFono, restarts WirePlumber, and prints the remaining
root\-only steps.
.TP
.B version
Print the version and exit.
.PP
Most commands accept
.BR \-v / \-\-verbose .
.SH ENVIRONMENT
Variables may also be set in the configuration file (see FILES), which
the daemon, the CLI and the systemd unit all read. Explicit environment
variables win.
.TP
.B IPHONEBRIDGE_MAC
The iPhone's Bluetooth address. Required;
.B pair-setup
writes it.
.TP
.B IPHONEBRIDGE_ADAPTER
Bluetooth adapter to use (default: hci0).
.TP
.B IPHONEBRIDGE_NOTIFY_EXPIRE_MS
How long message and app notifications stay on screen, in
milliseconds (default: 10000). 0 means never expire; dismissing a
message popup marks that message read on the iPhone, letting it expire
does not.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/iphonebridge/local.env
Configuration, one VAR=value per line.
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/iphonebridge/events.jsonl
Message and notification history (append\-only).
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/iphonebridge/contacts.sqlite
Contacts cache pulled over PBAP.
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/iphonebridge/deleted-keys.txt
Tombstones for locally deleted messages.
.PP
Paths honour XDG_CONFIG_HOME and XDG_STATE_HOME.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
iphonebridge sms-list -n 20
iphonebridge sms-list --from Maddie --source local
iphonebridge sms-send Maddie "running late"
iphonebridge call "1 (800) MYAPPLE"
journalctl --user -u iphonebridge -f
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR iphonebridge-ui (1),
.BR bluetoothctl (1),
.BR journalctl (1)
.PP
Full documentation and troubleshooting:
.UR https://github.com/santisbon/iphonebridge
.UE
.SH BUGS
Report at
.UR https://github.com/santisbon/iphonebridge/issues
.UE
